## Documented work

- **Emergency Research CMAX Fund (2017).** A fund created to research emergency assistance solutions with direct input from affected communities.
- **Social Innovation Lab for Emergencies, LISE (2018).** Created with Universidad de Monterrey. Its first workshop, "Innovation for prevention: strategic planning in earthquakes", took place in Oaxaca on 16 and 17 July 2018, after the September 2017 earthquakes. See [the case record](/our-actions/mexico-social-innovation-lab-for-emergencies).
- **Public-private network for disaster risk reduction, Mexico (2019).** A private-sector alliance for disaster resilience launched in January 2019. See [the case record](/our-actions/mexico-public-private-network-for-disaster-risk-reduction).

## What this program is not

CMAX Foundation does not run a standing training curriculum. Workshops and convenings are listed individually, with dates and participants, so that each one can be verified.
